   "source": [
    "## 5. Model Training\n",
    "\n",
    "Both models are built using scikit-learn **pipelines**. This ensures that preprocessing is fitted only on the training data and not on the validation or test data.\n",
    "\n",
    "### Logistic Regression\n",
    "- Uses One-Hot Encoding and **StandardScaler**.\n",
    "- Uses `max_iter=1000`.\n",
    "- Provides more interpretable results.\n",
    "\n",
    "### Random Forest\n",
    "- Uses One-Hot Encoding **without scaling**.\n",
    "- Uses **150 decision trees**.\n",
    "- Can capture complex and non-linear relationships.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Why scaling?** Logistic Regression needs scaling because the features have different ranges. Random Forest does not require scaling because it makes decisions based on feature splits.\n",
    "\n",
    "The cell below calls `train_models()` from `phoenix_ml.py` — the same function used by the Streamlit app."
   ]
  },
  {
