   "source": [
    "## 6. Model Evaluation\n",
    "\n",
    "Each model is scored on four metrics, all with respect to the **Leave** class:\n",
    "\n",
    "- **Accuracy:** share of all employees classified correctly. On a dataset that is 84% \"stay\", a model that predicts \"stay\" for everyone already scores 84%, so accuracy alone is not enough here.\n",
    "- **Precision:** of the employees flagged as leaving, how many actually left.\n",
    "- **Recall:** of the employees who actually left, how many were caught. This is the metric that matters most for retention — a missed leaver is a lost employee.\n",
    "- **ROC-AUC:** how well the model separates the two groups across all thresholds.\n",
    "\n",
    "The **validation set** We it  used to compare the models; the **test set** is used once for the final figure. Alongside the two models we score a **Combined Prediction** that averages their probabilities and flags anyone at 50% or above
   ]
  },
