   "source": [
    "### Why recall matters here — and why Random Forest recall is low\n",
    "\n",
    "Only **16.1%** of employees left, so a model can score high **accuracy** by mostly predicting \"stay\" while missing most leavers. For HR retention, **recall** matters more: every missed leaver is a lost employee we cannot intervene for. **Logistic Regression** catches more leavers because its linear boundary suits this dataset well. **Random Forest** has lower recall on the test set because, with few leave examples (~36 in 221 rows), its tree splits often favour the larger \"stay\" class unless class imbalance is handled (e.g. class weights or threshold tuning)."
   ]
  },
